ow many  do you believe they can reliably handle  well they ought to be able to reliably  handle  the ballots because it's only one ballot  per person  but what they're in the middle of doing  is making changes  to make it harder to deliver those  ballots as we've seen they're  they're scooping up mailboxes all over  the western united states for example  which rely already on vote by mail and  they're all other kinds of changes that  are being suddenly done  at the post office and you know many of  us don't have a view  necessarily of whether these changes  over the long run  are the right or wrong thing but they  are deeply misguided and  very suspicious coming at a moment when  the president who appointed this new  postmaster general  is saying he wants to block it from  delivering ballots to people  we all want to be just how the this  differs from state to state which states  rely more on mail and balloting  well uh seven states this is principally  how they vote that's out in the west  coast mostly  a lot of states have absentee balloting  and to be super clear there's no  difference between absentee ballots  and mail-in ballots there's a lot of  states where you have the ability to do  it but it has not been the case that  people  have needed to do it in such large  numbers uh  and so what states need to do is to  make sure people have the ability to get  those absentee ballots send out the  applications early  let people start sending in the ballots  early  and start counting early the whole goal  is to avoid chaos on election day so we  can have a meaningful and free  and fair and safe election michael is  there any way that the democrats can  sort of seize on the president's words  here at this point  and turn it around in this idea that the  people that rely on the postal service  the most right  now veterans the elderly people in rural  communities  they're the ones that need it the  president isn't funding it is it  something that they can seize on now 